# dovecot FHS migration: base runtime dir /run/dovecot -> /var/run/dovecot.
#
# --with-rundir moves the whole state tree (master pid, anvil/auth/
# dict/lmtp sockets), not just one file. The master starts as root
# and owns the directory lifecycle, so the dir stays root-owned
# 0755 (unchanged semantics, new namespace).
#
# Stale-state policy (/var/run is persistent by design, never wiped):
# - master.pid: tracked by supervise-daemon (OpenRC pidfile) and
#   systemd (PIDFile); a live second master is refused by the
#   daemon itself (anvil handshake), never by pidfile deletion.
# - State sockets: recreated by the master on start; stale files
#   from an unclean shutdown are reclaimed by the daemon.
#   No pid/socket cleanup in service logic.
# - New /var/run/dovecot: converged here on upgrade; created by
#   checkpath (OpenRC) and ExecStartPre (systemd).
# - Old /run/dovecot: volatile residue on tmpfs. Removed once
#   empty; left in place and reported while the old master runs.

dir /var/run/dovecot 0755 root root
rmdir-if-empty /run/dovecot
